# Who looks after which content. A pull request that changes a folder asks
# its owners for review, and the edit mode's GitHub sign-in will check the
# same lines before it opens one. The last line that matches a path wins,
# so every line names the super admins too.
#
#   Super admins: everything.
#   Town admins: towns/<town>/, the town's page and its public places.
#   Private admins: sites/<site>/, the site and its private places
#   (sites/<site>/places/).
#
# Add an admin by their GitHub login, for example:
#   /towns/rouge/        @schryer @rouge-admin
#   /sites/oobikuoru/    @schryer @oobikuoru-admin

*                        @schryer
